{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"plan","namespace":"","artifact_type":"","name":"P74e3c201"},"owner_reference":"#3332","content":"{\"plan_id\":\"P74e3c201\",\"feature\":\"docs-backlog-item-groomed-schema-field-drift\",\"version\":\"1.0.0\",\"description\":\"\",\"goal\":\"Correct six documented drift points in plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md so the doc's frontmatter fields, priority/status vocabularies, cross-reference link, and storage framing match backlog_core/models.py and the plugin's multi-backend design, with no other file modified.\",\"context\":\"**Implementation base SHA**: c3a455680f06d30a1286e64babd89d08d253969b\\n\\n\\n\\n### Discovered During Implementation\\n\\n_Session Date: 2026-08-31_\\n\\nDuring the quality-gate pass on #3332 (docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md field-drift fix), two findings emerged that were not part of the original context.\\n\\n**Key Discoveries:**\\n\\n1. **Single-file AC scope is structurally impossible for any `plugins/`-scoped commit**: `plugins/development-harness/.pre-commit-config.yaml:160-166` registers an `auto-sync-manifests` pre-commit hook (`files: ^plugins/`, `pass_filenames: false`) that unconditionally rewrites `plugin.json` version fields in `.claude-plugin/`, `.codex-plugin/`, and `.cursor-plugin/` on every commit touching any file under `plugins/`. T2 (feature-verifier) and the independent quality-gate code-review both confirmed this: the landed commit for this item touched 4 files, not the 1 the acceptance criteria required, and the same three-file bump pattern appears on the two commits immediately preceding it in repo history. A literal \\\"no other file changes\\\" acceptance criterion is unsatisfiable for any doc/code change under `plugins/` while this hook is active. Future items with a single-file-scope AC should either explicitly except hook-generated manifest version bumps in the AC wording, or the AC should be understood as \\\"no other *substantive* file changes.\\\"\\n\\n2. **The architect spec's own corrective text introduced a new inaccuracy**: Edit 2 of the architect spec (line 5 replacement) added the sentence \\\"passed through `backlog_groom(groomed_content=...)`.\\\" A post-merge doc-drift audit (2026-08-31, after this item's implementation and quality-gate review both passed) found `backlog_groom()` has no `groomed_content` parameter \\u2014 its actual signature (`backlog_core/server.py:2550-2616`) takes `selector`, `section`, `content`, `entry_id`, `replace_section`, `reason`, `append`, `sections`, `mark_groomed`. T1 applied the architect spec's text verbatim (correctly, per the plan's own instruction to not paraphrase), and both T2 and the independent code-review verified the nine acceptance criteria but none of them checked this specific function-signature claim against `server.py` because it was not one of the nine ACs. This is a genuine residual defect in the merged doc, not implementer error \\u2014 it demonstrates that an architect-authored \\\"corrected\\\" replacement paragraph needs the same fact-check rigor as the original defect it replaces, especially when it introduces new factual claims (like a function signature) that weren't in the original text being corrected.\\n\\n#### Updated Technical Details\\n\\n- `backlog_groom()`'s real signature (as of `backlog_core/server.py:2550-2616`): `selector`, `section`, `content`, `entry_id`, `replace_section`, `reason`, `append`, `sections`, `mark_groomed` \\u2014 no `groomed_content` parameter exists.\\n- The `auto-sync-manifests` pre-commit hook (`plugins/development-harness/.pre-commit-config.yaml:160-166`) fires on any commit touching `plugins/**` and bumps three plugin.json manifests; this is repo-wide behavior, not specific to this feature.\\n\\n#### Gotchas for Future Developers\\n\\n- Do not treat \\\"no other file changes\\\" acceptance criteria as literal-passing-or-failing for `plugins/`-scoped work without checking whether the manifest auto-sync hook fired; it always will.\\n- When an architect spec adds new factual claims (e.g. a function call signature) as part of a \\\"corrected\\\" replacement text \\u2014 not just removing wrong text \\u2014 verify those new claims against source before applying them verbatim, even though the plan otherwise instructs literal application of the spec's text.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"\",\"issue\":\"3332\",\"tasks\":[{\"id\":\"T1\",\"title\":\"Apply the six text corrections to docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"agent\":\"dh:task-worker\",\"dependencies\":[],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[],\"priority\":1,\"complexity\":\"low\",\"skills\":[],\"created\":\"2026-08-30T11:24:34.678027+00:00\",\"started\":\"2026-08-30T11:35:09.001319+00:00\",\"completed\":\"2026-08-30T11:37:19.244905+00:00\",\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"\",\"description\":\"Single atomic edit to one file. The six corrections are interdependent as a unit \\u2014 Edits 1 and 4 are the same `name`\\u2192`title` drift in two places and leave the doc self-contradictory if split; Edits 3 and 5 are adjacent lines in the same code fence. Apply them together in one diff.\\n\\n**Read first, in this order:**\\n1. `artifact_read(item_id=3332, artifact_type=\\\"architect\\\")` \\u2014 the exact before/after text for each edit. This is the authority. Apply the specified replacement text verbatim; do not paraphrase, reword, or 'improve' it.\\n2. The target file in full, so the surrounding structure is understood before editing.\\n\\n**Step 0 \\u2014 verify anchors before editing (do not skip).**\\nThe architect spec's line numbers were confirmed at commit `e0fb48d1e` with a clean worktree. Confirm they still hold before applying anything:\\n- `git status --porcelain` on the target file \\u2192 expect no pending modification.\\n- Confirm each anchor's *text* (not just its line number) is present and unedited: the `**Location**:` paragraph, the `(../../research/README.md)` link, `name: \\\"Item title\\\"`, `priority: P0|P1|P2|Ideas`, `status: open|in-progress|done|resolved`, and the `Do **not** duplicate \\\\`name\\\\`,` prose rule.\\n- If any anchor text differs from the architect spec's 'Current' block, STOP and report the divergence rather than guessing at an adapted edit. Line numbers may legitimately shift; the anchor *text* must match.\\n\\n**The six edits (summary only \\u2014 take exact text from the spec):**\\n1. `~:15` frontmatter `name:` \\u2192 `title:`\\n2. `~:5` `**Location**:` paragraph \\u2192 the `**Scope**:` paragraph defining the content-vs-storage boundary\\n3. `~:23` status vocabulary \\u2192 `open|done|in-progress|needs-grooming|closed`\\n4. `~:46` prose rule's `name` \\u2192 `title`\\n5. `~:21` priority vocabulary \\u2192 `P0|P1|P2|Ideas|completed`, with the annotation required by the constraint below\\n6. `~:11` link `../../research/README.md` \\u2192 `../../../research/README.md`\\n\\nEdits 2 and 6 sit above the others; apply from the bottom of the file upward, or re-locate each anchor by text immediately before editing it, so earlier edits do not invalidate later line numbers.\",\"objective\":\"Bring plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md into agreement with backlog_core/models.py and the plugin's multi-backend design by applying the six corrections specified in the #3332 architect spec, changing no other file.\",\"constraints\":\"- **One file only.** `git status --porcelain` at the end must list exactly `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md` and nothing else. AC #6 is a hard gate.\\n- **No unrequested improvements.** Do not restructure headings, reflow paragraphs, fix unrelated typos, or touch the `## Groomed` section table, the `:58` \\\"No line numbers\\\" rule, or the `:80` Issue #314 condition. Those are explicitly out of scope and were deliberately deferred.\\n- **Edit 5 annotation is required, not optional.** The architect spec leaves this as implementer judgment; this plan settles it \\u2014 write the line as:\\n  `  priority: P0|P1|P2|Ideas|completed  # \\\"completed\\\" is set internally on completion, not chosen by the groomer`\\n  Reason: `models.py:733-739`'s `VALID_NEW_ITEM_PRIORITIES` deliberately excludes `completed` from what a caller may request. Listing it unannotated would teach the groomer that `completed` is an authoring choice \\u2014 the identical defect class (an internal value presented as an authoring option) that this item fixes for `resolved` and `name`. The annotation still satisfies AC #7's exact-vocabulary-match requirement.\\n- **Edit 2's AGENTS.md citation must be plugin-scoped.** The architect spec's replacement paragraph reads `see \\\\`AGENTS.md\\\\` \\u00a7Backend Providers`, but its own Verification section notes the \\u00a7Backend Providers section lives in the **plugin-level** `plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md`, not the repo-root one. From the doc's location a bare `AGENTS.md` is ambiguous and would seed fresh drift. Write the citation as `plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md` \\u00a7Backend Providers.\\n- **Do not add `name` back in any form**, including as a documented legacy alias \\u2014 settled in plan context.\\n- **Do not add `reference:` to the frontmatter example** \\u2014 settled in plan context.\",\"expected_outputs\":\"- Modified: `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md` (six corrections, single file).\\n- A report of each verification step's actual output.\\n- Any divergence between the architect spec's 'Current' text and the file's real text, if found at Step 0.\\n- A `<concerns>` block for anything noticed but deliberately not fixed.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"Maps 1:1 to #3332's acceptance criteria. All must hold in the edited file:\\n- [ ] No `name:` field appears in the frontmatter example as a current schema element (item AC #1).\\n- [ ] The frontmatter example's fields match `BacklogItem` per `backlog_core/models.py:1011-1013` \\u2014 `title` and `description` at top level, `metadata:` block below (item AC #2).\\n- [ ] No single hardcoded per-item file path is presented as the universal storage mechanism (item AC #3).\\n- [ ] The storage/scope paragraph is true for all four backends (github, sqlite, memory, beads), or explicitly scopes backend-specific detail as such (item AC #4).\\n- [ ] The status vocabulary reads exactly `open|done|in-progress|needs-grooming|closed` \\u2014 every value in `_VALID_STATUSES` (`models.py:723`) present, `resolved` absent (item AC #5).\\n- [ ] `git status --porcelain` shows exactly one modified file (item AC #6).\\n- [ ] The `~:46` prose rule names `title`, not `name` (item AC #7).\\n- [ ] The priority vocabulary includes all of `P0`, `P1`, `P2`, `Ideas`, `completed` per `_VALID_PRIORITIES` (`models.py:721`), with the `completed` annotation from the constraints (item AC #8).\\n- [ ] The `~:11` link resolves to the repo-root `research/README.md` \\u2014 i.e. `../../../research/README.md` (item AC #9).\",\"verification_steps\":\"Run these after editing and report each result. Use absolute paths; the shell cwd resets between calls.\\n\\n1. **`name` fully eliminated as a current field:**\\n   `grep -n 'name' plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md`\\n   Expect: zero hits presenting `name` as a schema field. (Incidental prose such as \\\"function names\\\" at `:58` is fine and out of scope \\u2014 confirm any remaining hit is of that kind, not a field reference.)\\n\\n2. **Status vocabulary is canonical:**\\n   `grep -n 'status:' plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md`\\n   Expect the metadata line to contain `needs-grooming` and `closed`, and NOT `resolved`.\\n\\n3. **Priority vocabulary is canonical and annotated:**\\n   `grep -n 'priority:' plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md`\\n   Expect `completed` present with the trailing `#` annotation.\\n\\n4. **Vocabularies verified against source, not memory (