on\":\"defect\",\"analysis_method\":\"none\",\"divergence_notes\":0,\"accuracy_risk\":\"medium\"},{\"id\":\"T2\",\"title\":\"Independently verify all nine acceptance criteria and the single-file scope gate\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"agent\":\"dh:feature-verifier\",\"dependencies\":[\"T1\"],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[],\"priority\":1,\"complexity\":\"low\",\"skills\":[],\"created\":\"2026-08-30T11:24:34.678089+00:00\",\"started\":\"2026-08-30T11:41:51.422082+00:00\",\"completed\":\"2026-08-30T11:46:08.095418+00:00\",\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"\",\"description\":\"Independent verification pass. Do not re-read T1's self-report as evidence; verify against the file and its primary sources directly.\\n\\nThis exists as its own task because the item has no test surface (feature-context \\u00a7C1) \\u2014 nothing automated fails if a correction is wrong or a scope boundary was crossed. Goal-backward inspection is the only gate.\\n\\n**Read for the criteria:** `backlog_view(selector=\\\"#3332\\\", summary=False, sections=[\\\"Acceptance Criteria\\\"])` \\u2014 nine criteria across two entries. Also read `artifact_read(item_id=3332, artifact_type=\\\"architect\\\")` for the out-of-scope list.\\n\\nFor each criterion, state VERIFIED or GAP with the concrete evidence (grep output, file excerpt, or source-file line) that supports the verdict. A criterion you cannot check must be reported as such, never assumed satisfied.\",\"objective\":\"Confirm, working backward from #3332's nine acceptance criteria, that each is actually satisfied in the edited file \\u2014 and that no out-of-scope file or out-of-scope region of the target file was changed.\",\"constraints\":\"- **Read-only with respect to the fix.** Do not apply corrections yourself. Report GAPs; T1's owner or the orchestrator decides the remedy.\\n- **Verify against primary sources, not the spec's quotations.** Open `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py` and read `_VALID_STATUSES` / `_VALID_PRIORITIES` directly.\\n- **Scope regressions are failures, not nitpicks.** A correct set of six edits accompanied by a seventh unrequested edit fails item AC #6.\",\"expected_outputs\":\"- Per-criterion VERIFIED/GAP table with cited evidence for all nine criteria.\\n- Overall verdict: VERIFIED or GAPS_FOUND.\\n- A `<concerns>` block for anything observed but out of scope.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"- [ ] Each of #3332's nine acceptance criteria has an explicit VERIFIED or GAP verdict with cited evidence.\\n- [ ] `_VALID_STATUSES` and `_VALID_PRIORITIES` were read from `models.py` in this task and compared member-for-member against the doc.\\n- [ ] The full diff was reviewed and every hunk mapped to one of the six specified edits; any unmapped hunk is reported as a GAP.\\n- [ ] The out-of-scope regions (`## Groomed` section table, the `:58` \\\"No line numbers\\\" rule, the `:80` Issue #314 condition) are confirmed unmodified.\\n- [ ] `plugins/development-harness/templates/backlog-item.md` is confirmed unmodified.\\n- [ ] A single overall verdict of VERIFIED or GAPS_FOUND is returned.\",\"verification_steps\":\"1. `git diff --stat` \\u2192 confirm exactly one file changed, and record the line delta.\\n2. `git diff plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md` \\u2192 map every hunk to one of the six architect edits; flag any unmapped hunk.\\n3. `git status --porcelain` \\u2192 confirm no untracked or additionally-modified files.\\n4. Read the edited file in full and check each of the nine criteria by inspection.\\n5. `grep -n '_VALID_STATUSES\\\\|_VALID_PRIORITIES' plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py` \\u2192 read the literals; compare member-for-member with the doc's two vocabulary lines.\\n6. Confirm the `~:11` link's `../` depth is correct by counting directory levels from `plugins/development-harness/docs/` to the repo root, and confirm `research/README.md` exists at the root.\\n7. Confirm the storage/scope paragraph makes no assertion that is false for `sqlite`, `memory`, or `beads` \\u2014 read it against `plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md` \\u00a7Backend Providers.\\n8. Confirm the Edit 2 paragraph cites the plugin-level `AGENTS.md` path unambiguously (a bare `AGENTS.md` from this doc's location is ambiguous and is itself a fresh drift point).\",\"context_notes\":\"Expect the diff to be roughly six hunks, one file, near-zero net line change (Edit 2 replaces one paragraph with one paragraph of similar length \\u2014 the architect spec notes this explicitly, so a large line delta is itself a signal worth investigating).\\n\\nThe `~:46` occurrence of the `name`\\u2192`title` drift is the one most likely to be missed: it sits 30 lines below the frontmatter example and reads as prose rather than schema. Check it specifically.\\n## Verification Report (T2)\\n\\n**Overall verdict: GAPS_FOUND** \\u2014 8 of 9 criteria VERIFIED; AC #6 (single-file scope) is objectively violated by three hook-generated `plugin.json` version bumps in commit `5921eec17`.\\n\\nAll evidence gathered independently against primary sources; T1's self-report was not read.\\n\\n## Per-criterion verdicts\\n\\n| # | Criterion | Verdict | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Frontmatter no longer shows `name:` | VERIFIED | `grep -n 'name\\\\b' <doc>` \\u2192 zero matches. Line 15 now reads `title: \\\"Item title\\\"`. |\\n| 2 | Frontmatter matches `BacklogItem` fields (`models.py:1011-1013`) | VERIFIED | `models.py:1011-1013` = `title`, `reference`, `description`. Doc has `title` + `description`; `reference` omitted per architect Edit-1 Note (internally-managed collision field, not author-set). |\\n| 3 | Storage section drops the universal hardcoded per-item path | VERIFIED | Line 5 `**Location**` \\u2192 `**Scope**`; the `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/backlog/{priority}-{slug}.md` path and `dh_paths.backlog_dir()` call are gone entirely. |\\n| 4 | Storage claim holds for all four backends | VERIFIED | Line 5 names github/sqlite/memory/beads explicitly and declares storage format+location backend internals, citing `plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md` \\u00a7Backend Providers \\u2014 section confirmed present at `AGENTS.md:538-540`. Path is repo-root-relative, so unambiguous (T2 verification step 8 satisfied). |\\n| 5 | Status vocabulary == `_VALID_STATUSES` | VERIFIED | `models.py:723` = `{\\\"open\\\", \\\"done\\\", \\\"in-progress\\\", \\\"needs-grooming\\\", \\\"closed\\\"}`. Doc line 23 = `open\\\\|done\\\\|in-progress\\\\|needs-grooming\\\\|closed`. Member-for-member match; non-canonical `resolved` removed. |\\n| 6 | No other file changes | **GAP** | `git show --stat 5921eec17` \\u2192 4 files. Three unmapped: `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`, `.codex-plugin/plugin.json`, `.cursor-plugin/plugin.json`. See Gap detail below. |\\n| 7 | Line ~46 prose rule uses `title` not `name` | VERIFIED | Line 46: \\\"Do **not** duplicate `title`, `description`, `source`, \\u2026\\\". Confirmed by the same zero-match grep as #1. |\\n| 8 | Priority vocabulary == `_VALID_PRIORITIES` | VERIFIED | `models.py:721` = `{\\\"P0\\\", \\\"P1\\\", \\\"P2\\\", \\\"Ideas\\\", \\\"completed\\\"}`. Doc line 21 = `P0\\\\|P1\\\\|P2\\\\|Ideas\\\\|completed` plus the agreed trailing annotation. Annotation is corroborated by `models.py:733-739`, which excludes `completed` from `VALID_NEW_ITEM_PRIORITIES` for exactly the stated reason. |\\n| 9 | `:11` relative link resolves | VERIFIED | Line 11 now `../../../research/README.md`. From `plugins/development-harness/docs/` three levels up is the repo root; `ls plugins/development-harness/docs/../../../research/README.md` resolves to the real 238k file. |\\n\\n## Diff hunk mapping\\n\\n`git diff e0fb48d1e HEAD -- <doc>` \\u2192 **1 file, 6 insertions, 6 deletions**, matching the architect's predicted near-zero net delta. Every hunk maps to a specified edit; no unmapped hunk inside the target file:\\n\\n- Edit 1 \\u2192 line 15 `name:` \\u2192 `title:`\\n- Edit 2 \\u2192 line 5 `**Location**` paragraph \\u2192 `**Scope**` paragraph\\n- Edit 3 \\u2192 line 11 link depth `../../` \\u2192 `../../../`\\n- Edit 4 \\u2192 line 21 priority vocabulary + annotation\\n- Edit 5 \\u2192 line 23 status vocabulary\\n- Edit 6 \\u2192 line 46 prose `name` \\u2192 `title`\\n\\n## Out-of-scope regions confirmed unmodified\\n\\n- `## Groomed Sections` table (lines 62-81) \\u2014 present and untouched; no diff hunk in that range.\\n- \\\"No line numbers\\\" rule \\u2014 intact at line 58.\\n- \\\"When groomed after Issue #314\\\" condition \\u2014 intact at line 80.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/templates/backlog-item.md` \\u2014 `git log e0fb48d1e..HEAD -- <template>` returns empty. Unmodified.\\n- `git status --porcelain` \\u2192 clean; no untracked or additionally-modified files.\\n\\n## Gap detail \\u2014 AC #6\\n\\nCommit `5921eec17` changed three manifests beyond the target file:\\n\\n```\\n.claude-plugin/plugin.json   10.4.9 -> 11.0.1\\n.codex-plugin/plugin.json     9.4.9 -> 10.0.1\\n.cursor-plugin/plugin.json    6.4.9 -> 7.0.1\\n```\\n\\n**Cause is tooling, not authorship.** `.pre-commit-config.yaml:160-166` registers the `auto-sync-manifests` pre-commit hook (`plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/auto_sync_manifests.py`) with `files: ^plugins/` and `pass_filenames: false`. Any commit touching `plugins/` triggers it. The two preceding commits show the same pattern (`e0fb48d1e`: 10.4.8\\u219210.4.9; `1dbbd8208`: 10.4.7\\u219210.4.8), so a version bump accompanying a `plugins/`-scoped commit is the repository norm.\\n\\nAC #6 is nonetheless literally unsatisfied, and per this task's constraints scope regressions are reported as failures rather than waived. The remedy is an orchestrator/T1-owner decision \\u2014 the realistic options are to accept the bump as unavoidable hook output and amend AC #6's wording, or to revert the three manifest lines and commit with the hook bypassed (which would contradict the repo's own gate).\\n\",\"analysis_method\":\"none\",\"divergence_notes\":0,\"accuracy_risk\":\"low\"}],\"source_path\":null,\"state\":\"ready\"}"}